      "body": "Fixes #43434\n\n## Motivation\n\nA text-only `Gemma4ForCausalLM` export of Gemma 4 26B A4B (`model_type: gemma4_text`) fails to load, while the same weights load fine as `Gemma4ForConditionalGeneration`.\n\n`_apply_gemma4_attention_overrides` is what gives SGLang's Gemma 4 configs the full-attention shape on `head_dim` / `num_key_value_heads` and the sliding-window shape on `swa_*`. It only ran for the multimodal model types and always read `config.text_config`, so a text-only config never got it, and `gemma4_causal.py` built the global layers with the sliding-window head dim (256 instead of 512). That is the `Attempted to load weight (torch.Size([512])) into parameter (torch.Size([256]))` error in the issue.\n\nWith transformers 5.19 it fails even earlier: `get_hf_text_config` returns the config itself for a text-only checkpoint, and the loop that copies text-config attributes onto the config calls `hasattr` on the still heterogeneous `num_key_value_heads`, which raises `AmbiguousGlobalPerLayerAttributeError`.\n\n## Modifications\n\n* Add `gemma4_text` to `_GEMMA4_MODEL_TYPES`, and let `_apply_gemma4_attention_overrides` use the config itself when there is no `text_config`.\n* Skip the text-config attribute copy in `HfModelConfigParser.parse` when the text config is the config (there is nothing to copy).\n* Add `test_text_only_checkpoint_gets_the_same_overrides`, which saves a `Gemma4TextConfig` with different sliding and global shapes and loads it through `get_config`. It fails on `main` and passes with this change.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNot run: I don't have a GPU to load the 26B checkpoint end to end. The change only affects how the config is parsed for `gemma4_text`, and the multimodal path is unchanged.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\nUnit tests run locally (CPU): `test/registered/unit/utils/test_hf_transformers.py` and `test/registered/unit/configs/test_model_config.py` (92 passed), and every unit test file that mentions Gemma 4 (823 passed, 7 skipped).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38157665977](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38157665977)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38157665767](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38157665767)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38157666106](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38157666106)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
